From: liuqin Fedora adaptation <liuqin@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] liuqin 7.3.1: iris-clock-order

a9035926 / 9cfae772; disable all three 7.3 clocks before power domain.
Original-Author: Vishnu Reddy <busanna.reddy@oss.qualcomm.com>
Upstream-commit: https://github.com/yzddmr6/linux-sm8450-liuqin/commit/a90359262dacdd6efbb94de5c33c03b760586dc0
Signed-off-by: Vishnu Reddy <busanna.reddy@oss.qualcomm.com>
Signed-off-by: Bryan O'Donoghue <bod@kernel.org>
Linux-derived code retains original GPL notices. Offline port; no hardware claim.
---
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_vpu_common.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_vpu_common.c
@@ -223,10 +223,10 @@
 void iris_vpu_power_off_hw(struct iris_core *core)
 {
 	dev_pm_genpd_set_hwmode(core->pmdomain_tbl->pd_devs[IRIS_HW_POWER_DOMAIN], false);
-	iris_disable_power_domains(core, core->pmdomain_tbl->pd_devs[IRIS_HW_POWER_DOMAIN]);
 	iris_disable_unprepare_clock(core, IRIS_BSE_HW_CLK);
 	iris_disable_unprepare_clock(core, IRIS_HW_AHB_CLK);
 	iris_disable_unprepare_clock(core, IRIS_HW_CLK);
+	iris_disable_power_domains(core, core->pmdomain_tbl->pd_devs[IRIS_HW_POWER_DOMAIN]);
 }
 
 void iris_vpu_power_off(struct iris_core *core)
